qa-029: a subscription file written by hand, the way the inbox note shows
it — no id, created, or next_due (every = 1d, so the walker's 1h horizon
lets the kernel go idle after the first run). Expect: the kernel fills them in (id from
the file name, created from the mtime, due now), the command runs once
before the kernel goes idle, and the file is rewritten with the fields. A
second file with no cmd is not scheduled; the kernel log names it once.
State travels as dot-arbos/ (the repo ignores .arbos/); the runner renames it.
